.TH "nctetris" "1" "v3.0.17" ""
.SH "نام (NAME)"
nctetris \- Тетрис in the terminal
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\f[B]nctetris\f[R]\ [\f[B]\-h|\-\-help\f[R]]\ [\f[B]\-l\ loglevel\f[R]]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
\f[B]nctetris\f[R] implements a Tetris clone using Notcurses.
.PP
The goal is to complete horizontal lines, without allowing tetriminos to
reach the top of the screen.
The falling tetrimino can be rotated counter\- clockwise with the
\[aq]z\[aq] key, and clockwise with the \[aq]x\[aq] key.
The tetrimino can be moved left and right with \[aq]h\[aq] and
\[aq]l\[aq], respectively.
It can be moved down with \[aq]j\[aq].
The arrow keys can also be used.
Quit with \[aq]q\[aq].
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
\f[B]\-h\f[R]: Show help and exit.
.PP
\f[B]\-l loglevel\f[R]: Log everything (high log level) or nothing (log
level 0) to stderr.
.SH "نکات (NOTES)"
Optimal display requires a terminal advertising the \f[B]rgb\f[R]
terminfo(5) capability, or that the environment variable
\f[B]COLORTERM\f[R] is defined to \f[B]24bit\f[R] (and that the terminal
honors RGB escapes), along with a good fixed\-width font with good
coverage of the Unicode Block Drawing Characters.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\f[B]notcurses(3)\f[R]
.SH "نویسندگان (AUTHORS)"
nick black \c
.MT nickblack@linux.com
.ME \c.
